WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 14 Student Video
Unit 4, Lesson 2: Beauty

1
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.940
Think of the most beautiful thing you can imagine.

2
00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:24.120
Is it a rose, a snow-capped mountain, a rhythmic dance or a distant galaxy?

3
00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.320
For me, I think of Glacier Bay in Alaska.

4
00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:31.000
It's magnificent and it's truly beautiful.

5
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:35.800
I also think of the aqua colored water and the coral in the Caribbean.

6
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:39.680
Regardless of what came to your mind, I doubt any of you when I asked the question

7
00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:43.060
thought beauty, I don't believe there's real beautiful things in the world.

8
00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:48.860
the reality is we all actually believe in objective beauty and

9
00:00:48.860 --> 00:00:53.980
yet interestingly when asked most people would say they agree with the statement

10
00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:59.740
that beauty is in the eye of the beholder so which is it is beauty a

11
00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:04.500
real part of the world in which we live or is it entirely a matter of personal

12
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.700
preference like choosing an ice cream flavor if

13
00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:13.510
you find yourself agreeing with the statement that beauty is in the eye of the

14
00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:17.910
beholder, then you need to at least realize that you are in the minority in terms of

15
00:01:17.910 --> 00:01:23.770
history. That's right. Most thinkers from a variety of traditions have believed that

16
00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:28.450
there are three transcendentals that stand outside of human opinion.

17
00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:31.890
Goodness, truth, and beauty.

18
00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:38.350
And if beauty really exists, then there's good reason to believe there's a God or

19
00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:43.810
some kind of divine artist responsible for making the world beautiful you

20
00:01:43.810 --> 00:01:49.470
might be thinking wait a minute how can beauty be objective a real feature of the

21
00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:54.530
world when people differ over what they think is beautiful after all when it comes

22
00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:59.510
to music taste some people like rap other people like country when it comes to art

23
00:01:59.510 --> 00:02:04.450
some people like paintings of landscapes where other people like art that is more

24
00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:08.230
abstract. How can beauty be real when there's such disagreement?

25
00:02:08.570 --> 00:02:13.330
At first, this seems like a strong objection but keep a couple things in mind.

26
00:02:13.690 --> 00:02:17.830
First, nothing follows logically from disagreement.

27
00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:22.770
People disagree over all sorts of things but does that mean there's no truth?

28
00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:28.050
Take science and history. People differ over what is historically true and over what

29
00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:32.670
is scientific fact. does that mean there's no facts and there's no truth of course

30
00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:33.730
not we

31
00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:42.980
could spend all day arguing over which of these two flowers is most beautiful what

32
00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.300
would come of it probably not much but we would still agree that there's such a

33
00:02:47.300 --> 00:02:51.900
thing as beauty we would still agree that flowers can't possess that property and in

34
00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:56.040
fact we would agree that flowers many times really are beautiful

35
00:02:56.040 --> 00:03:00.040
Second, what do we do with disagreements?

36
00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:05.500
Music tastes, for example. There is still general agreement that certain rhythmic

37
00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:10.640
patterns, structures and arrangements are necessary for music to be beautiful.

38
00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:15.760
And while people may disagree over what particular features of a person are

39
00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:20.440
beautiful, there is agreement that human beings can truly be beautiful.

40
00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:26.720
The universal recognition of beauty in nature – crashing waves, a sunset or a rose –

41
00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:31.660
must not be missed even though we may disagree on the particulars we

42
00:03:33.970 --> 00:03:39.050
certainly speak as if we think beauty is objective when we say a rose is beautiful

43
00:03:39.050 --> 00:03:43.730
we speak as if we think there's some property or characteristic that that rose

44
00:03:43.730 --> 00:03:49.650
itself possesses when we talk about a poem being beautiful we seem to be indicating

45
00:03:49.650 --> 00:03:55.090
that we think there's a quality of the poem itself that is beautiful in other words

46
00:03:55.090 --> 00:04:00.550
when we say that something is beautiful we mean that that individual thing has the

47
00:04:00.550 --> 00:04:06.530
universal property of beauty so when i say to my wife you are beautiful i mean

48
00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:12.290
that she has a property of beauty that's something she possesses as a person

49
00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:17.530
and her beauty is just as real a feature of her as the fact that she has a certain

50
00:04:17.530 --> 00:04:22.690
height and a certain eye color you might not quite be fully convinced yet but you do

51
00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:27.350
have to admit that we at least speak as if we believe that beauty is real.

52
00:04:27.530 --> 00:04:32.970
So here's the question, can pantheism and naturalism adequately explain beauty?

53
00:04:44.790 --> 00:04:50.490
According to naturalism our ability to recognize beauty is some evolved trait that

54
00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.050
we inherited from our ancestors.

55
00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:58.330
Now first glance this might seem reasonable after all if a species of beings found

56
00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:02.410
their environment pleasing they would be more likely to survive, arguably.

57
00:05:02.770 --> 00:05:08.630
The problem is we don't just find the world pleasing, we find it beautiful.

58
00:05:09.010 --> 00:05:14.550
We explore the depths of the ocean and we peer into the most distant galaxies and we

59
00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:20.290
regularly find beauty. The world is filled with beauty but it's

60
00:05:20.290 --> 00:05:24.130
seemingly gratuitous beauty that has no survival value.

61
00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:29.850
What about pantheism? can it adequately explain beauty?

62
00:05:30.190 --> 00:05:33.990
As you will remember on pantheism, all is one.

63
00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:38.010
So there's really no distinctions in nature that are real.

64
00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:43.410
So what that means is there's no genuine difference between beauty and between

65
00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:48.510
ugliness. So rather than accounting for why we find beauty in nature,

66
00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:52.750
Pantheism simply explains beauty away as an illusion.

67
00:05:54.710 --> 00:05:58.070
The Christian worldview takes beauty seriously.

68
00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:04.270
Since God himself is beautiful and he has crafted the world with purpose and order,

69
00:06:04.510 --> 00:06:07.570
we should expect to find beauty in creation.

70
00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:10.570
And that is exactly what we find.

71
00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:16.830
The splendor of a waterfall, the magnificence of a diamond or the grandeur of a

72
00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:19.990
sequoia tree. the world is filled with beauty.

73
00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:25.170
Just take a look at the world around you, or even take out your smartphone and look

74
00:06:25.170 --> 00:06:29.530
at the photos. Our hearts resonate when we experience beauty.

75
00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:36.010
The existence of real beauty in the world may not prove that God exists, but it is

76
00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:41.450
one powerful pointer that the world has been fashioned with purpose, order, and

77
00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:44.070
beauty by a divine artist.

